  "id": "an-l2-delegation-with-architectureimpact-is-refused-until-th",
  "title": "An L2 delegation with architectureImpact is refused until the record carries an ARCH- decision",
  "requirement": "REQ-308 (AC-1..AC-3): an L2 change that declares architectureImpact does not start without the architect's decision recorded in the Analysis Record; the refusal carries a code and says what to write; the same delegation with the decision passes; L0, L1 and L2 without architectureImpact are unaffected.",
  "kind": "regression",
  "status": "superseded",
  "source": "agent",
  "automated": true,
  "testPath": "plugins/orchestrator/test/architect-consult-gate.test.mjs",
  "runCommand": "node --test plugins/orchestrator/test/architect-consult-gate.test.mjs",
  "steps": [
    "Mount the orchestrator with a fake board and the analysis service; call delegate_task with changeClass L2, architectureImpact true and analysisId architect-gate-and-plan-view, whose decisions[] holds no ARCH- entry.",
    "Call the same delegation with decisions[] carrying {id:\"ARCH-1\"}.",
    "Call L0, L1 and L2 without architectureImpact.",
    "Run architectConsultation against the real Analysis Record of this workspace, then against a copy of it with one ARCH- decision."
  ],
  "expected": "The first call returns {ok:false, code:\"architect_consult_required\"} with a message naming decisions[] and an ARCH- id, the components, invariants, checks and rollback path, and writes no task row and starts no child; the second creates one row and starts one child; L0/L1/L2-without-impact pass; the real record refuses and its copy passes.",
